From: Armada <noreply@armada>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: optional raster composite for the blit pass

The compute composite (cs_composite_blit) writes the output with imageStore,
which costs ~14.4 ms per 1080x2400 frame on Adreno 618 even at 750 MHz and
with coalesced rotated stores. Add an opt-in raster path for the plain blit
branch: a fullscreen triangle drawn with dynamic rendering into the output
image, with the same layer sampling, blending and colour management done in
a fragment shader. Rotation is applied by inverse-mapping gl_FragCoord to the
logical coordinate, so the result matches the compute path pixel for pixel.

Enable with GAMESCOPE_COMPOSITE_RASTER=1. Output images then also get
COLOR_ATTACHMENT usage (modifier selection is filtered by usage as before).
FSR/SGSR/NIS/blur passes and composite debug markers stay on compute.
The new pipelines are compiled on first use for the output view format.

While there, hoist the SDR colour chain out of the per-layer sampling path:
when every layer shares the same SRGB/LINEAR colourspace and has colour
management enabled, the shaper + 3D LUT are applied once after blending
instead of once per layer. LUTs that are already the identity are not bound
at all, which lets the composite shader drop the whole chain.
